  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying the outcome with minimum absolute value (sure outcome), computing weighted differences from that value, and summing them to compare lotteries. The individual did not mention the minimum absolute value or any differences from it. Instead, the individual focused only on the probability of the zero outcome as a proxy for risk. While both lotteries have a zero outcome, the individual did not apply the structured rule of the decision reason (i.e., identifying the sure outcome and summing weighted differences). The justification is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as described. The reasoning is qualitatively different and does not reflect the computational structure of the reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
